# Seating Arrangements for Orientation Day

**Author:** Samuel Mensah  
**Date Finalized:** March 24, 2026

## Overview
This document outlines the finalized seating arrangements for the orientation day scheduled to take place on **March 30, 2026**. The arrangements were meticulously planned to ensure a smooth and welcoming experience for all participants, including newly enrolled students, faculty, and staff.

## Objectives
The seating arrangements were organized with the following goals in mind:

- **Maximize Comfort:** Ensure all attendees have adequate space and seating.
- **Optimize Accessibility:** Prioritize seating arrangements for students and guests requiring special accommodations.
- **Facilitate Interaction:** Arrange seating to foster engagement between students, faculty, and staff.
- **Streamlined Organization:** Ensure ease of navigation within the venue.

---

## Venue Details

- **Location:** Main Auditorium, Campus Center
- **Capacity:** 1,200 seats
- **Setup Type:** Theater-style seating
- **Backup Venue (if needed):** Multipurpose Hall, Building B

---

## Seating Breakdown

### Section A - Front Rows
- **Reserved for:** Executive team, keynote speakers, and faculty.
- **Capacity:** 50 seats.
- **Special Requirements:** Additional legroom and accessibility for faculty members with mobility aids.

### Section B - Middle Rows
- **Reserved for:** First-year students (newly enrolled).
- **Capacity:** 600 seats.
- **Special Notes:**
  - Students will be seated alphabetically by last name.
  - Rows will be clearly labeled for easy identification.

### Section C - Back Rows
- **Reserved for:** Returning students, second-year and above.
- **Capacity:** 400 seats.
- **Special Notes:**
  - Seating is first-come, first-served.

### Section D - Side Rows
- **Reserved for:** Guests and family members.
- **Capacity:** 150 seats.
- **Special Requirements:**
  - Family units will be seated together.

---

## Accessibility Arrangements

- **Wheelchair Spaces:** 25 designated spots spread across all sections.
- **Assistive Listening Devices:** Available at the venue entrance for attendees with hearing impairments.
- **Sign Language Interpreters:** Positioned near the front rows.
- **Mobility Assistance:** Staff will be stationed at key points to guide attendees with special needs.

---

## Entry and Exit Flow

- **Entry Points:**
  - Main auditorium entrance (north side).
  - Secondary entrance (west side).

- **Exit Points:**
  - Emergency exits located at the rear and sides of the auditorium.

- **Directional Signage:** Clearly visible signs will guide attendees to their assigned sections.

---

## Staff Assignments

### Event Coordinators
- **Responsibilities:** Overseeing seating arrangements and resolving any issues on-site.
- **Assigned Personnel:**
  - Jessica Tan
  - Ahmed Patel

### Ushers
- **Responsibilities:** Guiding attendees to their seats.
- **Assigned Personnel:**
  - 20 trained student volunteers.

### Technical Team
- **Responsibilities:** Setting up AV equipment and ensuring smooth operation.
- **Assigned Personnel:**
  - Chris Daniels
  - Monica Li

---

## Contingency Plans

- **Overflow Seating:** Multipurpose Hall will serve as an overflow venue, with live video streaming of the event.
- **Emergency Protocols:**
  - First aid stations will be set up near the main entrance.
  - Security teams will be on standby to assist in case of emergencies.

